{"paper": "SSC-DelhiPoliceHC-27-Oct-2022-Shift1.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "sequential", "splitter": "qdot", "section_slice": true, "extracted_count": 25, "tagged_count": 25, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 2, "text": "A company offers the following: I. Successive discounts of 25% and 5% II Successive discounts of 20% and 10% III Successive discounts of 22% and 8% Which offer is the best for a customer?", "options": [{"text": "III", "added": false}, {"text": "All are equally good", "added": false}, {"text": "II", "added": false}, {"text": "I", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "successive-discounts", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 3, "text": "If the radii of two circles be 8 cm and 6 cm and the length of the transverse common tangent be 14 cm, then the distance between the two centres is:", "options": [{"text": "8√3 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "16√3 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "28√2 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "14√2 cm", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Circles-Polygons", "sub": "tangents-and-chords", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 4, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "surds-and-indices", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 5, "text": "A policeman follows a thief 1800 metres ahead of him. If the policeman and the thief run at a speed of 12 km/h and 9 km/h, respectively, how much distance thief will cover from spotting point (1800 meters ahead to policeman) before catch by policeman?", "options": [{"text": "5600 metres", "added": false}, {"text": "6000 metres", "added": false}, {"text": "4200 metres", "added": false}, {"text": "5400 metres", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Speed-Distance", "sub": "relative-speed", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 6, "text": "For a certain sum, the amount received after 2 years at 18% p.a. simple interest is Rs.1,100 less than the simple interest on the same sum for 10 years at the same rate. The sum (in Rs.) is:", "options": [{"text": "Rs.2,400", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs.2,300", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs.2,500", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs.2,200", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simple Interest", "sub": "si-formula", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 7, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "−3.18", "added": false}, {"text": "−1.18", "added": false}, {"text": "5.28", "added": false}, {"text": "1.18", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 8, "text": "When the price of an article was reduced by 20%, its sale increased by 80%. What was the net effect on the revenue?", "options": [{"text": "Decreased by 21%", "added": false}, {"text": "Increased by 21%", "added": false}, {"text": "Increased by 44%", "added": false}, {"text": "Decreased by 44%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "successive-change", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 9, "text": "Two years ago, population of a city was 15,62,500. The population increased by 4% in the first year and decreased by 4% in the second year. Find the present population", "options": [{"text": "15,60,000", "added": false}, {"text": "15,61,000", "added": false}, {"text": "15,63,000", "added": false}, {"text": "15,62,000", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "population-and-depreciation", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 10, "text": "Find the value of z in (z × 21% of 210) ÷ (17% of 170) = 3050 ÷ z", "options": [{"text": "18.4", "added": false}, {"text": "44.7", "added": false}, {"text": "22.1", "added": false}, {"text": "33.1", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "basic-percentage", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 11, "text": "What is mean proportion between 361 and 144?", "options": [{"text": "121", "added": false}, {"text": "264", "added": false}, {"text": "288", "added": false}, {"text": "228", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "proportion", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 12, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Sequences and Series", "sub": "arithmetic-progression", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 13, "text": "P and Q together can finish a piece of work in 4 days. If P alone can finish the work in 12 days, then what are the number of days required for Q alone to finish the work?", "options": [{"text": "4 days", "added": false}, {"text": "6 days", "added": false}, {"text": "5 days", "added": false}, {"text": "8 days", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "together-apart", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 14, "text": "A shopkeeper professes to sell his goods at the cost price, but he uses false weights with which he cheats by 10% while buying and by 15% while selling. His overall percentage of profit or loss is:", "options": [{"text": "5%", "added": false}, {"text": "27.7%", "added": false}, {"text": "22.72%", "added": false}, {"text": "25%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "dishonest-dealer", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 15, "text": "The average runs made by a batsman in 10 innings of cricket was 43. How many runs does he have to make in the next inning so that the average of his runs increases by 3?", "options": [{"text": "83", "added": false}, {"text": "76", "added": false}, {"text": "78", "added": false}, {"text": "91", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Average", "sub": "replacement-effect", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 16, "text": "The length (in cm) of the transverse common tangent to two circles of radii 2 cm and 5 cm, the centre of the circles being 8 cm apart, is:", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Circles-Polygons", "sub": "tangents-and-chords", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 17, "text": "A,B & C can all together do a piece of work in 20 days, in which B takes 4 times as long as A & C to do the work and C takes 3 times as long as A & B together take to do the work. In how many days B can alone do the work?", "options": [{"text": "120 days", "added": false}, {"text": "80 days", "added": false}, {"text": "90 days", "added": false}, {"text": "100 days", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "together-apart", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 18, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 19, "text": "If the base of an equilateral triangle is 8 cm, then find its area.", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 2D", "sub": "triangle-and-quadrilaterals", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 20, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "30", "added": false}, {"text": "36", "added": false}, {"text": "50", "added": false}, {"text": "14", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Circles-Polygons", "sub": "tangents-and-chords", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 21, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Coordinate Geometry", "sub": "area-and-centroid", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 22, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "linear-equations", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 23, "text": "A vessel is in the form of a hollow hemisphere mounted by a hollow cylinder. The diameter of the hemisphere is 14cm and the total height of the vessel is 13cm. What is the inner surface area of the vessel?", "options": [{"text": "172 cm2", "added": false}, {"text": "572 cm2", "added": false}, {"text": "372 cm2", "added": false}, {"text": "772 cm2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cylinder", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 24, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "85", "added": false}, {"text": "78", "added": false}, {"text": "89", "added": false}, {"text": "80", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "bar-graph", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 25, "text": "What is the total surface area of a cone with diameter of 42 cm and height of 20 cm?", "options": [{"text": "3600 cm2", "added": false}, {"text": "3900 cm2", "added": false}, {"text": "3000 cm2", "added": false}, {"text": "3300 cm2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cone", "key_answer": null}]}